00:53:02.320 --> 00:53:04.040
I don't have too much more to say.

00:53:04.240 --> 00:53:05.360
I don't think it's essential.

00:53:05.540 --> 00:53:06.660
But the biggest thing right away,

00:53:06.840 --> 00:53:09.240
barring it, is the way it controls for me

00:53:09.240 --> 00:53:10.660
and the way the enemies come in and stuff.

00:53:10.760 --> 00:53:14.680
I mean, all the other stuff is kind of icing on the not essential cake.

00:53:16.080 --> 00:53:17.240
But yeah, I mean,

00:53:17.620 --> 00:53:19.200
it wasn't the worst game we've played.

00:53:19.320 --> 00:53:20.240
I can say that. Great.

00:53:20.380 --> 00:53:22.760
And you know what? I'll take a slice of that cake while you're at it

00:53:22.760 --> 00:53:25.180
because I also think that this game is not essential,

00:53:26.020 --> 00:53:27.440
mostly for the controls thing.

00:53:27.820 --> 00:53:29.940
But I think there's just a,

00:53:30.020 --> 00:53:31.540
there's a lack of understanding

00:53:31.540 --> 00:53:34.600
in what could have made this game good from Data East.

00:53:34.760 --> 00:53:35.980
And this is now like,

00:53:36.100 --> 00:53:36.900
I don't even know,

00:53:37.080 --> 00:53:38.560
the eighth or ninth game from them

00:53:38.560 --> 00:53:39.960
that we're just straight up rejecting.

00:53:40.480 --> 00:53:41.900
So they really need to,

00:53:41.900 --> 00:53:43.860
they just need to chill for a second

00:53:43.860 --> 00:53:45.480
and just think about it.

00:53:45.760 --> 00:53:47.000
Now that gets into a whole conversation,

00:53:47.000 --> 00:53:49.860
of course, about whether game companies even care

00:53:49.860 --> 00:53:52.360
if the games are good or not at this point,

00:53:52.560 --> 00:53:53.780
as long as they sell, right?

00:53:53.940 --> 00:53:55.720
Like if you're in a limited market

00:53:55.720 --> 00:53:57.100
where only a certain amount of games

00:53:57.100 --> 00:53:58.160
are coming out each month,

00:53:58.400 --> 00:54:00.280
you have a great amount of the share

00:54:00.280 --> 00:54:02.080
in what's available to anybody.

00:54:02.200 --> 00:54:04.020
So I'm sure a lot of it just went into

00:54:04.020 --> 00:54:05.400
like making sure that like

00:54:05.400 --> 00:54:07.940
the back of the box looked cool enough

00:54:07.940 --> 00:54:08.960
so that you would buy it.

00:54:09.100 --> 00:54:10.020
And then, then later,

00:54:10.300 --> 00:54:11.820
you know, like where any kids take a note?

00:54:12.060 --> 00:54:13.760
Like, oh, I didn't like Karate Champ.

00:54:13.840 --> 00:54:16.260
That game sucked. I'm not going to buy the next Data East game.

00:54:16.280 --> 00:54:17.720
I wonder how many people thought about that

00:54:17.720 --> 00:54:20.000
because we don't have video game magazines yet either.

00:54:20.080 --> 00:54:20.940
But that's a whole nother story.

00:54:21.240 --> 00:54:22.080
But I say,

00:54:22.260 --> 00:54:23.820
Data East, you're not getting away with this.

00:54:24.000 --> 00:54:25.060
We will remember you.

00:54:25.640 --> 00:54:27.540
Sean? Yeah,

00:54:27.760 --> 00:54:29.580
you guys covered it pretty well.

00:54:29.580 --> 00:54:31.900
I think that this is just a,

00:54:32.020 --> 00:54:34.880
I don't think that there was any direct relationship

00:54:34.880 --> 00:54:37.680
because I think that the arcade game

00:54:37.680 --> 00:54:39.260
came out before Mega Man.

00:54:39.400 --> 00:54:42.680
But this is just like a shoddy Mega Man to me

00:54:42.680 --> 00:54:45.860
in terms of the tools

00:54:45.860 --> 00:54:48.500
are sort of like your power-ups in Mega Man

00:54:48.500 --> 00:54:52.020
and the shoot first nature of it.

00:54:53.880 --> 00:54:56.240
It's just not a fun game to play.

00:54:56.540 --> 00:54:57.880
It's too hard for its own good.

00:54:57.880 --> 00:54:59.580
It's random. It's janky.

00:54:59.720 --> 00:55:01.080
It's not essential.

00:55:01.540 --> 00:55:02.400
And there you have it.

00:55:02.640 --> 00:55:03.660
Three votes as a no

00:55:03.660 --> 00:55:05.120
means that there's no way

00:55:05.120 --> 00:55:08.380
that Karnov is getting on the essential games list.

00:55:08.500 --> 00:55:11.260
That's going to mean that Karnov will not be

00:55:11.260 --> 00:55:12.860
on the essential games list.

00:55:12.860 --> 00:55:15.640
And so we start off 1988 0 for 1.

00:55:16.040 --> 00:55:18.400
But next week we have Renegade,

00:55:18.540 --> 00:55:20.660
which is made by Technos Japan.

00:55:20.900 --> 00:55:22.660
So maybe they'll give us something.

00:55:24.840 --> 00:55:26.320
Any insights on that?

00:55:26.520 --> 00:55:27.640
I also hope it's good.

00:55:27.640 --> 00:55:29.520
Yeah, good. I hope it's good as well.

00:55:29.720 --> 00:55:31.560
And then we actually have another big game

00:55:31.560 --> 00:55:33.180
coming up for if you're looking in the forecast.

00:55:33.480 --> 00:55:35.520
Two episodes from now we have Contra,

00:55:36.080 --> 00:55:38.820
which I'm sure a lot of our listeners are fans of.

00:55:39.000 --> 00:55:40.920
Personally, I've never played a Contra,

00:55:41.080 --> 00:55:42.400
so I'm excited.

00:55:42.740 --> 00:55:45.220
I just know the Vampire Weekend album, Contra.

00:55:45.680 --> 00:55:47.580
So I've aged myself out of this.

00:55:47.620 --> 00:55:53.220
What about the anti-government forces in Nicaragua?

00:55:53.420 --> 00:55:55.300
Is that what Contra, the video game,

00:55:55.340 --> 00:55:56.880
is a reference to? Maybe.

00:55:57.200 --> 00:56:00.340
Cool. I'm excited to do some anti-stuff.

00:56:02.560 --> 00:56:04.780
I am anti-stuff.

00:56:05.680 --> 00:56:06.600
You've heard it here.

